course: dictionary
lesson: 5830
title: Mainland and islands
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The mainland is the big, main part of a country or continent. It does not count the islands near it. When you read about a ferry going from an island to the mainland, the clue is in the words: «The ferry carried the children from the island back to the mainland.» The ferry is going to the big land, not to another small island.
explain: Look for the word island nearby. If the text compares an island with the land next to it, the mainland is the land next to it. In geography, Tasmania is an island, and mainland Australia is the large land beside it. Ask yourself: is this the big main land, or a small piece of land in the sea?
explain: Mainland is often used with another word, like mainland Europe or mainland China. Here the word tells you which big land is meant. The phrase back to the mainland means returning from the islands to the main land.
fact: The mainland is the main large part of a country or continent.
fact: An island is land with water all around it, and the mainland is the big land near the islands.
fact: «The Isle of Wight» is an island off the coast of mainland Britain.
fact: «Tasmania» is an island, and «mainland Australia» is the big land next to it.
fact: Mainland can be a noun, as in «the mainland», or an adjective, as in «a mainland town».
exercise: «The ferry sailed from the island back to the mainland.» Where did the ferry go? | *The big main land, not counting the islands | A harbour on a lake | An island far out at sea | The sky above the sea
exercise: «The Isle of Wight» is an island. Which phrase means the big land next to it? | The Isle of Wight | The sea | A ferry | *Mainland Britain
exercise: What does mainland mean in «mainland Europe»? | A boat that carries people | A tall hill by the coast | *The main large part of Europe, not counting its islands | A small island in the sea
test: Which word means the main large land, not counting the islands near it? | Harbour | Island | *Mainland | Ferry
test: Complete the sentence: The boat took the children back to the ___, leaving the island behind. | sand | sea | *mainland | cliff
exam: In geography, what does mainland mean? | A boat that carries people across the sea | *The main large part of a country or continent, not counting the islands near it | A small island in the middle of a lake | A tall hill by the coast
